  "term": "depressor nerve",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, the depressor nerve is described as a branch of the vagus that carries signals from an overfilled left ventricle to the medulla, leading reflexly to widening of blood vessels and easing pressure on the heart. It is presented as part of the heart’s influence on vascular tone.",
